      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OSHLEY (3) is a talented filly first up from a break of 11 weeks who generally comes to hand quickly, recording two wins and a placing from three fresh attempts. Last seen in the Queensland Oaks after recording a series of top-two finishes at Menangle. She draws well and will be ready to go off two trials. PERFECTDELIGHT (9) was making her first appearance since the Queensland Oaks when she scored at this venue, getting home by 2.4 metres after leading. That was three weeks ago but she was kept up to the mark with a trial. Draws for a trail and if she gets the gaps could be hard to hold out. SEASIDE DRIVE (2) drew wide and worked so wasn't disgraced in the city last time. Better drawn here and had won two of her previous three attempts. COCOS DESIRE (10) draws on the back row for her first outing in five months but she was a city winner three back and has been readied with two trials, winning the latest.",
